From 96ac73f0cf8263b187237c0d7ea9aecff73f783a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: u <u@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:07:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: ole2: fix 64-bit conversions in the interface thunks

- STATSTG16.pwcsName is a SEGPTR on _WIN64 (ole2 and storage ifs.h).
- Declare map_pformatetc16_32/32_16, take a SEGPTR in map_vardesc32.
- HTASK_32 gives a thread id; HFONT/HRGN are 16-bit handles in the
  16-bit interfaces; HOLEMENU16 entry points take HGLOBAL16.
- Fix MAP_LPCRECTL32_16 mapping the uninitialised 16-bit value.
- HGLOBALStreamImpl16_CopyTo passed a flat buffer to IStream16_Write;
  pass a mapped SEGPTR.
- Use 0 instead of NULL for SEGPTR values, drop pointer casts on
  16-bit vtable entries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ole2/hglobalstream.c | 11 +++++++----
 ole2/ifs.h           |  4 ++++
 ole2/ifs_thunk.c     | 30 ++++++++++++++++--------------
 ole2/ifs_thunk.h     | 14 ++++++++------
 ole2/memlockbytes.c  |  6 +++---
 ole2/ole2.c          | 20 ++++++++++----------
 storage/ifs.h        |  4 ++++
 storage/storage.c    |  4 ++++
 8 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)

